{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.PiL2","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finite"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.orthogonal_channels_le_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.orthogonal_channels_le_dim","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L91-L105","doc":"**Spatial-dimension bound.** In `ℝ³` a family of pairwise-orthogonal\nnonzero vectors has at most three members: orthogonal nonzero vectors are\nlinearly independent, and a linearly independent family in a space of\n`finrank` 3 has cardinality `≤ 3`. Embedding bond channels as mutually\northogonal directions, the number of channels — the bond order — is capped\nby the spatial dimension, so no bond exceeds order three. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bond-order-le-three","label":"prop:bond-order-le-three","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/bond-order-le-three.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.multipleBond_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.multipleBond_binding","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L82-L89","doc":"Order-`(m+1)` bond energy: `baseσ · (1 + m·w)`. For `w = 1` (equal\nchannels) this is `baseσ · (m+1)`; a lateral weight `w < 1` reduces it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.multipleBond_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.multipleBond_length","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L76-L80","doc":"The channel count of an order-`(m+1)` bond is `m+1` — the bond order —\nindependent of the overlap weight `w`: weighting changes only the energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.multipleBond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.multipleBond","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L70-L74","doc":"An order-`(m+1)` bond: one axial σ channel and `m` transverse π channels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.totalBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.totalBinding","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L66-L68","doc":"Overlap-weighted total binding of a composite of embeddable operators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.transverse_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.transverse_binding","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L59-L62","doc":"A transverse channel binds at `base · w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.axial_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.axial_binding","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L55-L57","doc":"An axial channel binds at its full base binding (`w = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.transverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.transverse","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L47-L53","doc":"A transverse (π-type) operator with lateral overlap `0 < w ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.axial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.axial","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L40-L45","doc":"An axial (σ-type) operator: full head-on overlap `w = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.binding","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L36-L38","doc":"Embedded binding contribution: base binding scaled by the overlap weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.weight_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.weight_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L32-L32","doc":"The overlap weight does not exceed the axial (head-on) maximum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.weight_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.weight_pos","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L30-L30","doc":"The overlap weight is positive: the channel binds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.overlapWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.overlapWeight","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Geometric overlap weight set by the embedding direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.baseBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.baseBinding","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L26-L26","doc":"Un-embedded channel binding (energy units). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.EmbeddableKnotOperator","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean#L21-L32","doc":"A knot operator embedded into the ambient 3-manifold with a geometric\noverlap weight `w ∈ (0, 1]`. Axial (σ-type) channels have\n`overlapWeight = 1`; transverse (π-type) channels have `overlapWeight < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}